Z||000026||Elenor84||12-11-2001||01:45 AM||||K this is the easiest thing in the world.  Grab the window...bend it back(don't worry these fiero's can take it), reach in and unlock it.  Vwola!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000027||fieroX||12-11-2001||03:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>K this is the easiest thing in the world.  Grab the window...bend it back(don't worry these fiero's can take it), reach in and unlock it.  Vwola!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thats what I did when I locked my keys in my car a few weeks ago.  But a little different.  My arms are pretty big, so I used a 1/2" drive breaker bar, and used the part that attaches to the sockets to slide the lock piece over.  Took me about 5 minutes to figure something out to make it work.<P>------------------<BR>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">  </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A><BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe||||reg||1
